<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Twenty-fourth Dynasty of Egypt</h1><p class="st-meta">732 BCE – 720 BCE (approx.) · capital Sais</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The brief Saite kingdom of Tefnakht and Bakenranef, which challenged the Kushites for control of Egypt.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tefnakht">Tefnakht</a>, Great Chief of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/libu">Libu</a> and the Ma at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sais">Sais</a> in the western Delta, united much of the Delta and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-egypt">Middle Egypt</a> in the 720s BCE. His advance south provoked the invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piye">Piye</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kushite-empire">Kushite Empire</a> around 728 BCE, after which Tefnakht submitted but kept his power and took royal titles.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Its kings controlled the western Delta and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/memphis-egypt">Memphis</a> and drew on the wealth of Delta trade with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bakenranef">Bakenranef</a>, called Bocchoris by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greeks">Greeks</a>, was remembered in Greek tradition as a wise lawgiver who reformed contract law. A vase with his name found in an Etruscan tomb at <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/tarquinii">Tarquinia</a> shows Saite trade links.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Around 720 BCE the Kushite king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shabaka">Shabaka</a> conquered the Delta; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manetho">Manetho</a> says he burned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bakenranef">Bakenranef</a> alive. The Saite family survived as local rulers and re-emerged as the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/twenty-sixth-dynasty-of-egypt">Twenty-sixth Dynasty of Egypt</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/twenty-fourth-dynasty-of-egypt.jpg" alt="Twenty-fourth Dynasty of Egypt" width="320" height="427"><figcaption>Image: Tilemahos Efthimiadis · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tefnakht_Athens_stela_(T._Efthimiadis).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>732 BCE – 720 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/8th-century-bce">8th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Sais</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Tefnakht, Bakenranef</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Ancient Egyptian religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Egyptian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/egypt">Egypt</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Twenty-fourth Dynasty, Saite kingdom of Tefnakht</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-726&amp;focus=twenty-fourth-dynasty-of-egypt" aria-label="Twenty-fourth Dynasty of Egypt on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5476 1049 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Twenty-fourth Dynasty of Egypt lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5796 1305L5862 1746"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5862 1746h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5796 1305h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5796 1305h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Sais. <a href="/atlas?year=-726&amp;focus=twenty-fourth-dynasty-of-egypt">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

